{"term":"muddy","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1b1ff8489d53af127c","definition":"Covered or splashed with, or full of, mud (“wet soil”).","example":"He slogged across the muddy field.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["oozy","clatchy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["muddily","muddiness","muddyish","Muddy Mississippi","Muddy York","nonmuddy","unmuddy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:72dbc7c66ea0a355ca","definition":"Of water or some other liquid: containing mud or (by extension) other sediment in suspension; cloudy, turbid.","example":"The previously limpid water was now muddy as a result of the struggle between the alligator and the wild boar.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["muddily","muddiness","muddyish","Muddy Mississippi","Muddy York","nonmuddy","unmuddy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:20e3e8aff9d6944d54","definition":"Of or relating to mud; also, having the characteristics of mud, especially in colour or taste.","example":"[H]er garments, heauy vvith her drinke, / Pul'd the poore vvretch from her melodious buy^([sic – meaning lay]), / To muddy death.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["muddily","muddiness","muddyish","Muddy Mississippi","Muddy York","nonmuddy","unmuddy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d5813db6b9c1dc00e0","definition":"Soiled with feces.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"euphemistic","register":"euphemistic","wordFamily":["muddily","muddiness","muddyish","Muddy Mississippi","Muddy York","nonmuddy","unmuddy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a77d6d1d7119260093","definition":"Of an animal or plant: growing or living in mud.","example":"There is a point of strand / Near Vada's tower and town; and on one side / The treacherous marsh divides it from the land, / Shadowed by pine and ilex forests wide, / And on the other creeps eternally, / Through muddy weeds, the shallow, sullen sea.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":["muddily","muddiness","muddyish","Muddy Mississippi","Muddy York","nonmuddy","unmuddy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cbbe3f4e4843eaf8fe","definition":"Dirty, filthy.","example":"There's not the ſmalleſt orbe [in the sky] vvhich thou beholdſt, / But in his motion like an Angell ſings, / Still quiring to the young eide Cherubins; / Such harmony is in immortall ſoules, / But vvhilſt this muddy veſture of decay [i.e., the human body] / Doth groſſely cloſe in it, vve cannot heare it.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["muddily","muddiness","muddyish","Muddy Mississippi","Muddy York","nonmuddy","unmuddy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muddy#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c44ecbe6b0a86ad4c7","definition":"Not clear.","example":"To vvhat, my loue, ſhall I compare thine eyne? / Chriſtall is muddy.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms"